# Web Lesson 52 -- finite trace, feedback, and traced-coverage boundary.
# visual: svg
# loops: 0
# ***************************************************************************
# * PREREQUISITES -- typed semantic graphs, tensor, composition, feedback.
# * CATEGORICAL SETTING -- one deterministic process p: A tensor U to B tensor U.
# * LAW -- explicit U feedback and trace-U have the same external endpoint.
# * BOUNDARY -- missing sliding evidence blocks a traced-category claim.
# * WHAT THIS SHOWS
# * Close only the designated U pair; keep A input and B output external.
# ***************************************************************************
;
include "lib/finite_trace_feedback.mlpl"  # reuse trace and coverage checks
feedback_typed = u:feedback_ports_are_compatible(["U"], ["U"])  # CT118
feedback_mismatch = 1 - u:feedback_ports_are_compatible(["U"], ["V"])  # COUNTEREXAMPLE
trace_endpoint = u:trace_matches_explicit_feedback([8], [8])  # CT116
changed_trace_endpoint = 1 - u:trace_matches_explicit_feedback([8], [9])  # COUNTEREXAMPLE
missing_law_coverage = 1 - u:traced_law_coverage_is_complete([1, 1, 0])  # CT117 boundary
disp([feedback_typed, feedback_mismatch, trace_endpoint, changed_trace_endpoint, missing_law_coverage])
# ***************************************************************************
# * THE VISUAL
# * Blue loops U output to U input; green arrows mark the external A-to-B path.
# ***************************************************************************
def u:finite_trace_feedback_web_visual() {
  "Render the shared finite trace, feedback, and law-coverage visual.";
  u:finite_trace_feedback_visual()
}  # narrated visual entry point
finite_trace_feedback_visual = u:finite_trace_feedback_web_visual()  # bind visual constant
finite_trace_feedback_visual  # display bound visual once
